IMPORT prelude

-- Skills and Workforce Development Agency Act 2026 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for a training provider, an employer, a
-- trainee or anyone else who meets the Agency's incentives, grants and loans: abusive funding arrangements and who "facilitates"
-- them (ss 49, 50), the mandatory penalty and the court's repayment order (ss 50(2), 51, 58(4)), false or misleading course
-- advertisements (s 52), the refund direction when a funded course is cancelled or stops (s 54), the appeal to the Minister
-- (ss 55, 56), the maximum punishments and the cap on composition (ss 8(2), 35(2), 50-54, 58-60), officers' liability for a corporation's
-- offence (s 61), and when service by registered post or email takes effect (s 64).
--
-- Edition: Act No. 17 of 2026, informal consolidation ("version in force from 1/7/2026", per the page footer), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SWDAA2026.txt (retrieved 1 October 2026, "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"). The deposit carries
-- no amendment annotations and no legislative history; s 1 says the Act comes into operation on a date the Minister appoints by
-- Gazette notification, and the deposit does not state that date. The section numbers are the body's: the enforcement provisions
-- are in Part 7 (ss 45-59) and the general provisions in Part 8 (ss 60-66).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0218 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. SCOPED to Parts 7 and 8 as they bear on people and businesses. Not encoded: the Agency's
-- establishment, functions, powers, membership, meetings, staff and finance (Parts 2 to 6), except the maximum punishments in
-- ss 8(2) and 35(2); the verification and inspection
-- powers of ss 46-48 beyond the obstruction offence; s 53's notice-and-decision procedure beyond the offence; unincorporated
-- associations and partnerships (s 62, which mirrors s 61); codes of practice (s 66); the transfer of SSG and WSG staff,
-- records and property, the repeal of the two predecessor Acts and the consequential amendments (Parts 9 to 11).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown in the example rows. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Skills and Workforce Development Agency Act 2026 -- funding`

-- s 60(1)(a), (b) need "the lower of" two sums; the prelude's min is not used.
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `49 -- abusive funding arrangement`

-- s 49(1): a "funding arrangement" is "any agreement, scheme, transaction or series of transactions (whether or not legally
-- enforceable) where the purpose, or one of the purposes, is to obtain an incentive, a grant or a loan from the Agency".
-- (2): it is ABUSIVE if it "results or would result in a person obtaining -- (a) an incentive, a grant or a loan from the Agency
-- that a person would otherwise not be eligible for or would not have obtained ...; or (b) an amount ... higher than what a person
-- would have been eligible for or would have obtained without that arrangement or transaction".
GIVEN `one purpose is to obtain Agency funding` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it gets funding otherwise not available` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it gets more funding than otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement is an abusive funding arrangement` IF
    `one purpose is to obtain Agency funding`
    AND (`it gets funding otherwise not available` OR `it gets more funding than otherwise`)

-- s 49(3): the "amount of wrongly obtained funding" (a) "is the amount of the incentive, grant or loan that results or would result
-- from the abusive funding arrangement ...; but (b) excludes any amount the person would have obtained without that abusive funding
-- arrangement or transaction". The floor at zero is an inference: the text does not contemplate a negative amount.
GIVEN `the funding resulting` IS A NUMBER, `the funding without the arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the wrongly obtained funding` MEANS
    IF `the funding resulting` GREATER THAN `the funding without the arrangement`
    THEN `the funding resulting` MINUS `the funding without the arrangement`
    ELSE 0

§§ `50(5), (6) -- who facilitates an arrangement`

-- s 50(5): a person facilitates if the person is (a) "a training provider or an employer who designs, organises or manages" it;
-- (b) an employee of that training provider or employer "who participates in, or by the employee's act or omission enables or
-- aids" it; (c) "a person who, by attending a course or programme, participates in, enables or aids" it; (d) "a marketing agent
-- who publishes, disseminates or communicates any information ... for the purpose of inducing or encouraging" others to enter
-- it; or (e) any other person who does any of those things.
-- (6): "However, a person does not facilitate ... only by reason that the person in the ordinary course of business -- (a)
-- provides services relating to, or provides connections for, the transmission or routing of data; (b) provides, or operates
-- facilities for, online services or network access; or (c) provides a service that" lets end-users communicate or publish.
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a training provider who designs the arrangement`
    `an employer who organises the arrangement`
    `an employee of the training provider who helps run it`
    `a trainee who attends the course to make it work`
    `a marketing agent who promotes it`
    `a friend who recruits trainees into it`
    `an internet provider routing the data`
    `a messaging app carrying the messages`
    `an online platform hosting the posts`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person facilitates the arrangement` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `an internet provider routing the data` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a messaging app carrying the messages` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an online platform hosting the posts` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `50(1), (7), (8) -- the offence`

-- s 50(1): an offence if the person "(a) enters into or facilitates a funding arrangement that is an abusive funding arrangement;
-- (b) knows or has reason to believe that [it] is an abusive funding arrangement; and (c) intends ... to dishonestly or
-- fraudulently induce the Agency to give an incentive, a grant or a loan to the person, or to any other person".
-- (7): the intention in (1)(c) "is presumed, until the contrary is proved" if the arrangement "involves any step or steps (other
-- than under subsection (6)) which is or are capable of assisting" anyone in it to obtain the funding.
-- (8): "it is not a defence ... that the accused did not obtain any incentive, grant or loan from the Agency". Whether anything
-- was obtained is therefore not an input.
GIVEN `entered into or facilitated it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it is abusive` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or had reason to believe it was abusive` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the dishonest intent is proved` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it involves a step capable of helping obtain funding` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the accused proves no such intent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abusive arrangement offence is committed` IF
    `entered into or facilitated it`
    AND `it is abusive`
    AND `knew or had reason to believe it was abusive`
    AND (    `the dishonest intent is proved`
         OR  (`it involves a step capable of helping obtain funding` AND (NOT `the accused proves no such intent`)))

§§ `51(3) -- where recovered money goes`

-- s 51(3)(c): where the funding came from a combination of the Skills Development Fund and the Agency's general moneys, "the
-- recovered amount must be paid into the Skills Development Fund and to the general moneys of the Agency in the respective
-- proportions that moneys were withdrawn" from each. (a) and (b) are the cases where one of the two is zero.
GIVEN `the amount recovered` IS A NUMBER, `drawn from the Fund` IS A NUMBER, `drawn from general moneys` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the share paid into the Skills Development Fund` MEANS
    `the amount recovered` TIMES `drawn from the Fund` DIVIDED BY (`drawn from the Fund` PLUS `drawn from general moneys`)

§§ `8(2), 35(2), 50(2), 52(2), 53(7), 54(8), 58(2), 59(2), 60 -- punishments and composition`

-- Two offences outside Parts 7 and 8 are included for the composition cap: s 8(2), using the Agency's symbol without written
-- permission or a deceptively similar one, "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months";
-- and s 35(2), disclosure of information by a member, officer, authorised person or inspector, "$2,000 ... 12 months".

-- s 50(2)(b): "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both", on top of the
-- mandatory penalty in (2)(a). s 52(2): "$5,000 ... 6 months". s 53(7)(a): "$10,000 ... 12 months", and (b) "a further fine not
-- exceeding $1,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". s 54(8): "$10,000 ...
-- 12 months". s 58(2): "$10,000 ... 12 months". s 59(2): "$5,000 ... 6 months".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `entering into or facilitating an abusive arrangement`
    `a false or misleading advertisement`
    `ignoring a direction about an advertisement`
    `ignoring a refund direction`
    `a false statement or document`
    `obstructing an officer or inspector`
    `using the Agency's symbol without permission`
    `an officer disclosing information in breach of secrecy`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `a false or misleading advertisement` THEN 5000
    WHEN `obstructing an officer or inspector` THEN 5000
    WHEN `an officer disclosing information in breach of secrecy` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `entering into or facilitating an abusive arrangement` THEN 36
    WHEN `a false or misleading advertisement` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing an officer or inspector` THEN 6
    WHEN `using the Agency's symbol without permission` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the advertisement direction offence can cost` MEANS
    10000 PLUS 1000 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 50(2)(a): on conviction the person "shall ... pay a penalty equal to the amount of wrongly obtained funding that the person
-- obtained, or would have obtained", and (3) it is "irrelevant" whether it was for the person's own benefit or another's.
GIVEN `the funding resulting` IS A NUMBER, `the funding without the arrangement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a conviction under s 50 can cost` MEANS
    (`the wrongly obtained funding` `the funding resulting` `the funding without the arrangement`) PLUS 10000

-- s 60(1): an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" may be compounded for "a sum not exceeding the lower of ... (a) one
-- half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $2,000". Which offences are prescribed is left
-- to regulations, which were not retrieved; this gives the cap if the offence is prescribed.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap` MEANS
    `the lower of` ((`the maximum fine` `the offence`) DIVIDED BY 2) 2000

§§ `52 -- false or misleading advertisements`

-- s 52(4): an advertisement is false or misleading in a material particular if it "(a) falsely represents that a person is
-- eligible for, or has been given, an incentive, a grant or a loan from the Agency in respect of a course or programme; (b)
-- falsely represents that the Agency has accredited ... a provider ...; (c) ... a course or programme; (d) falsely represents that
-- a provider ... or a course or programme, is approved or endorsed by the Agency; (e) contains any false or misleading information
-- concerning a provider ... who is eligible for, or has been given, an incentive, a grant or a loan ...; or (f) concerns a course
-- or programme in respect of which a person is eligible for, or has been given, [funding], and contains any false or misleading
-- description of ... (i) the curriculum, modules or subjects ...; or (ii) the competencies, expertise or skills to be advanced".
-- Whether the list is exhaustive is not said ("is false or misleading ... if"); this rule asks only whether a claim is within it.
DECLARE Claim IS ONE OF
    `falsely says the course attracts an Agency grant`
    `falsely says the Agency accredited the provider`
    `falsely says the Agency endorsed the course`
    `misdescribes the modules of a funded course`
    `overstates the skills a funded course teaches`
    `misdescribes the modules of an unfunded course run by an unfunded provider`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim falls within s 52(4)` IF
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `misdescribes the modules of an unfunded course run by an unfunded provider` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 52(1): an offence if the person "(a) ... publishes or causes to be published, or distributes or causes to be distributed, any
-- advertisement that is false or misleading in a material particular; and (b) ... knows or ought reasonably to have known that,
-- or is reckless as to whether," it is.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim,
      `published or distributed it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ought reasonably to have known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `was reckless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the false advertisement offence is committed` IF
    `published or distributed it`
    AND (`the claim falls within s 52(4)` `the claim`)
    AND (`knew` OR `ought reasonably to have known` OR `was reckless`)

§§ `54 -- refund when a funded course is cancelled or stops`

-- s 54(9): the "default day" is "(a) if subsection (1)(c)(i) applies [the course does not start on the scheduled starting day] --
-- the scheduled starting day ...; or (b) if subsection (1)(c)(ii) applies [it ceases after it starts but before it is completed]
-- -- the day on which the course or programme ceases to be provided". Days are day numbers.
GIVEN `the course never started` IS A BOOLEAN, `the scheduled starting day` IS A NUMBER, `the day it ceased` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the default day` MEANS
    IF `the course never started` THEN `the scheduled starting day` ELSE `the day it ceased`

-- s 54(1): the section applies where (a) the Agency has given funding to the provider (the "funding recipient") in connection
-- with the course; (b) the trainee takes part or intends to; (c) the course "(i) does not start on the scheduled starting day; or
-- (ii) ceases to be provided at any time after it starts but before it is completed"; and (d) "the trainee has not withdrawn from
-- the course or programme before the default day".
-- (7): the direction "applies despite anything to the contrary contained in any agreement between the funding recipient and the
-- trainee" or a person who paid for the trainee. So a no-refund term changes nothing.
GIVEN `the provider received Agency funding for the course` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the course never started` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the course stopped before completion` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the trainee withdrew` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the withdrawal day` IS A NUMBER,
      `the scheduled starting day` IS A NUMBER,
      `the day it ceased` IS A NUMBER,
      `the contract says no refunds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Agency may direct a refund` IF
    `the provider received Agency funding for the course`
    AND (`the course never started` OR `the course stopped before completion`)
    AND (    (NOT `the trainee withdrew`)
         OR  `the withdrawal day` AT LEAST (`the default day` `the course never started` `the scheduled starting day` `the day it ceased`))

-- s 54(2)(a): the refund to the trainee is "of the money received by the funding recipient before the default day". A payment
-- received on or after the default day is outside it.
GIVEN `the payment` IS A NUMBER, `the day it was received` IS A NUMBER, `the default day of the course` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refundable part of a payment` MEANS
    IF `the day it was received` LESS THAN `the default day of the course` THEN `the payment` ELSE 0

§§ `55, 56 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 55(2): an appeal "must be -- (a) in writing and specify the grounds on which it is made; and (b) made within 14 days (or any
-- other period of time that may be prescribed in substitution) after the date the direction appealed against is given". (3): the
-- Minister "may reject" an appeal that does not comply -- MAY, not must. s 56(2): the Minister's decision "is final". s 56(4):
-- the direction "must be complied with until the determination of the appeal" unless the Minister directs otherwise.
GIVEN `the day the direction was given` IS A NUMBER, `the day of the appeal` IS A NUMBER, `in writing with grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal complies with s 55(2)` IF
    `in writing with grounds`
    AND `the day of the appeal` AT LEAST `the day the direction was given`
    AND `the day of the appeal` MINUS `the day the direction was given` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `an appeal is pending` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the direction must be complied with now` IF
    (NOT `an appeal is pending`) OR (NOT `the Minister directed otherwise`)

§§ `61 -- officers of a corporation`

-- s 61(2): where a corporation commits an offence, an officer (or an individual involved in its management and in a position to
-- influence the conduct) who "(i) consented or connived, or conspired with others ...; (ii) is in any other way ... knowingly
-- concerned in, or is party to, the commission of the offence ...; or (iii) knew or ought reasonably to have known that the
-- offence ... would be or is being committed, and failed to take all reasonable steps to prevent or stop" it, "shall be guilty of
-- that same offence". (5): this applies "whether or not the corporation is convicted".
GIVEN `is an officer or influential manager` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `consented, connived or was knowingly concerned` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to stop it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is guilty of the same offence` IF
    `is an officer or influential manager`
    AND (    `consented, connived or was knowingly concerned`
         OR  (`knew or ought to have known` AND (NOT `took all reasonable steps to stop it`)))

§§ `64 -- service of documents`

-- s 64(5): service "takes effect -- (a) if the document is sent by email, at the time that the email becomes capable of being
-- retrieved ...; and (b) if the document is sent by prepaid registered post, 2 days after the day the document was posted (even
-- if it is returned undelivered)". (7): email or electronic-notice service "may be effected only with the person's prior written
-- consent". For personal delivery the section states no time; taking it as the day of delivery is an inference.
DECLARE Method IS ONE OF
    `by hand`
    `by registered post`
    `by email`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method, `the day sent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day service takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `by registered post` THEN `the day sent` PLUS 2
    OTHERWISE `the day sent`

GIVEN `the method` IS A Method, `prior written consent to email service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the method of service is allowed` IF
    CONSIDER `the method`
    WHEN `by email` THEN `prior written consent to email service`
    OTHERWISE TRUE
